WEBVTT

00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,600
Is a plant-based or alkaline diet best for the treatment for cancer?

00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:12,560
We get that question a lot. Should I go on a keto diet? Because oh my gosh, I read this book on

00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:18,640
keto diets and cancer. Should I go on a plant-based diet? Should I not do any animal protein whatsoever?

00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:23,760
Should I become a vegan or a vegetarian? Is that the best thing? Should I go on an alkaline diet?

00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:34,240
Is that the best thing? The truth is that cancer needs a growing cancer. So cancer is cells

00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:38,800
and rapid replication. That means they're highly metabolic. That means they're very hungry.

00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:44,800
So they're looking for a fuel source. Is that fuel source always strictly glucose?

00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:50,880
The answer is no. Sometimes it's not glucose. Sometimes it's glutamated,

00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:57,600
serrated, and those are different amino acids that are for protein. So a person whose

00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:06,320
cancer is driven mainly through amino acids, that is the main fuel source, then yes, a plant-based

00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:13,920
diet would be best for that person. But a plant-based diet, let's say, a typical

00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:19,600
like Gershon, Juicy, I'm going to start Juicy right away. Well, Juicy can be high in glucose.

00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:25,440
So your cancer is mainly through glycolysis through the breakdown of glucose, then that might

00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:34,320
not be the right diet. So how do I know? Because there's these extreme ends of ketogenic,

00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:42,720
which is very, very low sugar, very, very low glucose, but maybe higher

00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:54,320
the aspect of proteins versus a Juicy Gershon type diet, which is very high in glucose.

00:01:54,320 --> 00:02:00,880
So it's just, it's very difficult to know which one, which diet is best for you. So in our clinic,

00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:07,520
we test for that. But let's say you don't come to our clinic. How do I know what diet is best for me?

00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:16,640
There is some data out there on metabolic typing. That's what Dr. Gonzales used to do,

00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:23,120
is do metabolic typing, and he did produce some literature on that that you could take a very

00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:29,600
long questionnaire and get an idea of what could possibly be fuel in your cancer. We have found that

00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:38,880
to not be extremely effective in knowing what can fuel my cancer. Also, the struggle with that is

00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:44,960
that cancer is constantly trying to survive and fight a fuel source. So if your fuel source in your

00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:50,800
cancer is mainly glucose, and you go on a ketogenic like diet, don't have to necessarily get total

00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:57,280
and totally into ketosis, but if you go on a ketogenic like diet and you're starving, your cancer,

00:02:57,280 --> 00:03:03,680
that's the goal. But your cancer can switch quite easily because it's trying to find a fuel source

00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:10,720
and it can be fueled through a different pathway. So diets for cancer patients may need to switch

00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:18,080
over time. So if your cancer is fed mainly through amino acids and you cut down on the animal proteins

00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:23,280
and you find that your cancer is starting to go into revision and then six months later it starts to take

00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:28,320
off again. What's the matter? I've been staying on my diet. It might be because the fuel source switched.

00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:33,840
So if you're not a patient of ours and you don't have a way to find out what's the best diet for me,

00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:41,280
maybe a balanced diet, maybe low in animal proteins, doesn't mean you're going to go off them completely

00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:48,560
and get rid of all your simple carbs and try to get on a low carb diet. That is what we call a mixed diet.

00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:59,520
Most people that we test, honestly test positive for dairy being a driver for cancer. So I would

00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:09,680
suggest in general dietary cutting out dairy or cutting down dairy to a minimal is beneficial and

00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:15,840
it really has to do with the sort what dairy is. And we're talking about what comes out of a

00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:23,680
cow's udders. We're talking about dairy. What dairy is is to make a baby cow grow quickly and

00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:29,120
gain weight quickly and become an adult cow. So it has growth factors in there, it has hormones in

00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:34,400
there, it has all sorts of other impurities in there as well. Even organic dairy still has hormones

00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:39,920
and growth factors in it because that's what dairy is supposed to do. So that I would say in general

00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:47,360
is the right diet to do. But if you don't have a way to test it, the only way to test it really is to

00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:54,640
try one of these diets and see if it slows your cancer growth. Of course you have to have some

00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:59,520
in these subjective or objective data to be able to measure if you're slowing the cancer growth. But

00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:05,360
that's one way to do it is try a diet, see how you're doing, you're doing real well. If you're like

00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:10,720
you're in a relative state of remission, then stay on that diet. If things change in your cancer,

00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:16,640
wake up and start to grow it again, then think about switching diets because it's looking for a fuel

00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:17,600
source.

